 "notes": "Boundary of the hatched exclusion region in Fig. 4 (constraint on g_agamma vs ALP mass), extracted from the ROOT vector EPS (fig4.eps) path. Axes: x = m_a in units of 1e-12 eV (log, tick '1'@px272, '10'@px1914); y = g_agamma in units of 1e-11 GeV^-1 (log, tick '1'@px1331, minor ticks 0.4-0.9 give 2467 px/decade). Flat part at 8.3e-12 GeV^-1 reproduces the paper's quoted 95% CL limit g_agamma<8.3e-12 GeV^-1 for m_a below 7e-12 eV. The bump near ~7.6e-12 eV (up to ~9.9e-12) is the 'small range around 8e-12 eV where the exclusion is slightly less constraining' noted in the text; at higher masses the curve rises ~m_a^2, exiting the right frame edge at (1.4e-11 eV, 1.6e-11 GeV^-1). Not a DM search (spectral-irregularity method), so density-independent.",
